  "id": "absolute-pitch",
  "term": "absolute pitch",
  "definition": "Absolute pitch is the ability to identify a musical note directly from the sound itself, without relying on its relationship to other notes or a tonal context. In the source, it is described as an automatic, stimulus-driven way of coding pitch and is presented as uncommon.",
